  function traverseAndTest(node) {
    if (cache.has(node)) return; // Skip nodes that have been checked before to prevent redundant checks.

    cache.add(node); // Add node to the cache

    if (test(node)) results.push(node); // Test node and add matching elements to results

    node = node.firstChild;
    while (node) {
      traverseAndTest(node); // Recursively check child nodes
      node = node.nextSibling;
    }
  }

  traverseAndTest(element);
  return results;
}
```

To handle real-time updates, you can use a MutationObserver to monitor for changes in the DOM and clear the cache when necessary:

```javascript
const observer = new MutationObserver((mutations) => {
    mutations.forEach(() => cache.clear()); // Clear cache on each change detected by the observer
});

observer.observe(element, { childList: true, subtree: true });
```
The `MutationObserver` interface provides the ability to watch for changes being made to the DOM tree. When a change occurs in the observed element or its children, the callback is invoked with a list of MutationRecord objects as input. 

Remember that real-time updates will impact performance. Ensure your observer's settings and handling of cache clearing are optimized for better efficiency.
"]

