['Here's a simple implementation in Java using some concepts from concurrent programming and resource management to meet the requirements:

```java
import java.io.File;
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;
import java.util.concurrent.locks.ReentrantLock;

public class ThemeCacheManager {
    private final ConcurrentHashMap<String, ReentrantLock> locks = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    private final FileSystemAbstraction fsLayer;

    public ThemeCacheManager(FileSystemAbstraction fsLayer) {
        this.fsLayer = fsLayer;
    }

    public Bitmap getThemeBitmap(String themeName) throws Exception {
        ReentrantLock lock = locks.computeIfAbsent(themeName, k -> new ReentrantLock());

        try {
            if (lock.tryLock()) {
                // Assume bitmaps are stored in memory or can be loaded from fsLayer
                Bitmap themeBitmap;

                if ((themeBitmap = cache.get(themeName)) == null) {
                    File pngFile = new File(fsLayer.getCacheRoot(), themeName + ".png");
                    // Parsing a PNG file to bitmap for simplicity
                    themeBitmap = BitmapFactory.decodeStream(new FileInputStream(pngFile)); 

                    if (themeBitmap == null) {
                        throw new Exception("Unable to parse PNG theme file: " + pngFile);
                    }

                    cache.put(themeName, themeBitmap);
                }

                return themeBitmap;
            } else {
                throw new Exception("Theme is in use by another thread.");
            }
        } finally {
            lock.unlock();
        }
    }

    public void recycleAndNullify(String themeName) {
        ReentrantLock lock = locks.get(themeName);

        if (lock != null && lock.isHeldByCurrentThread()) {
            Bitmap bmp = cache.remove(themeName);

            if (bmp != null) {
                bmp.recycle();
            }
        } else {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Theme is not in use by current thread.");
        }
    }

    // Assume that fsLayer provides a consistent and reliable interface for 
    // accessing files, including cloud storage options.
}
```
In this code we are using `ConcurrentHashMap` for managing concurrent access to the theme cache. A `ReentrantLock` is used per theme to ensure that only one thread at a time can modify a particular theme bitmap. This prevents data corruption and supports multiple users. 

The code also integrates with an existing `FileSystemAbstraction` layer, which would manage both local storage and cloud storage options as needed. This allows the application to support varying network conditions and different device capacities.
']

