```java
import java.io.*;
import java.util.Date;
import java.lang.Runtime;
import java.nio.file.*;

public class Main {
    private static final String LOG_FILE = "log.txt";

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Example usage: command is "ls" or any other command
        executeCommand("ls");
    }

    /**
     * Execute a command and log details to a file for auditing purposes. 
     * The program should also delete an existing file before executing the command.
     */
    public static void executeCommand(String command) {
        Path path = Paths.get("test.txt"); // replace with actual file path

        try {
            Files.deleteIfExists(path);

            Process process = Runtime.getRuntime().exec(command, null, null);
            logExecutionDetails(process, command);

            BufferedReader stdInput = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(process.getInputStream()));
            BufferedReader stdError = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(process.getErrorStream()));

            String s;
            while ((s = stdInput.readLine()) != null) {
                System.out.println("stdout: " + s);
            }

            while ((s = stdError.readLine()) != null) {
                System.err.println("stderr: " + s);
            }
        } catch (IOException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }

    /**
     * Log command execution details to a file for auditing purposes.
     */
    public static void logExecutionDetails(Process process, String command) throws IOException {
        FileWriter writer = new FileWriter(LOG_FILE, true); // append mode

        Date startTime = new Date();
        long pid = process.pid();
        int exitValue = -1;

        try {
            exitValue = process.waitFor();
        } catch (InterruptedException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }

        Date endTime = new Date();

        writer.write("Command: " + command + "\n");
        writer.write("Start Time: " + startTime + "\n");
        writer.write("End Time: " + endTime + "\n");
        writer.write("PID: " + pid + "\n");
        writer.write("Exit Value: " + exitValue + "\n\n");

        writer.close();
    }
}
``` 

This program uses `java.lang.Runtime` to execute the command and get its output and error streams as `InputStreamReader`s. These are then wrapped in `BufferedReader`s for efficient reading of large files. The logging mechanism writes execution details (command, start time, end time, PID, exit value) to a file named "log.txt" in the current working directory.

Please note that this program has no error handling or input validation beyond deleting an existing file and writing logs. It's recommended to use a library like Apache Commons IO or Guava for command line argument sanitization and other production grade code practices. Also, please handle the exceptions properly in a real-world application.
