using System.Runtime.Serialization.Formatters.Binary;

public static class DataLoader
{
    public enum CompressionMethod { None, GZip, Deflate }

    public static T LoadData<T>(string filePath, CompressionMethod compression)
    {
        if (!File.Exists(filePath))
            throw new FileNotFoundException("The specified file was not found.", filePath);

        using (var fs = new FileStream(filePath, FileMode.Open))
        {
            Stream decompressed;

            switch (compression)
            {
                case CompressionMethod.GZip:
                    decompressed = new GZipStream(fs, CompressionMode.Decompress);
                    break;

                case CompressionMethod.Deflate:
                    decompressed = new DeflateStream(fs, CompressionMode.Decompress);
                    break;

                default:  // None or unsupported compression
                    fs.Position = 0;
                    decompressed = fs;
                    break;
            }

            var formatter = new BinaryFormatter();
            T data = (T)formatter.Deserialize(decompressed);

            if (!ValidateData<T>(data))
                throw new InvalidDataException("The deserialized data is corrupted or invalid.");

            return data;
        }
    }

    // Dummy validation method, replace with real one.
    private static bool ValidateData<T>(T data) => true; 
}
```
This code provides a basic implementation that loads binary data from a file and deserializes it using the BinaryFormatter class. The function supports three types of compression: None, GZip, or Deflate. If an unsupported compression method is used, the function falls back to loading raw data without decompression.

To validate the integrity of the deserialized data, a dummy validation method `ValidateData` has been provided that should be replaced with a real implementation specific to your requirements. In case of any errors during the file opening, decompression, or data validation process, an appropriate exception is thrown. 

