This code uses a mutex to ensure thread safety, preventing race conditions from multiple instances of the function running at the same time. The list is created by allocating new nodes and linking them together. Memory allocation failures are handled gracefully by printing an error message and exiting with a failure status. A random seed is used to generate the payload sizes, ensuring different results each run. Please note that this code assumes `generateRandomMacAddress` and `generateRandomPayload` functions have been implemented according to your needs.
