    for(size_t i=0; i<node->numChildren; ++i) {
        traverse(node->children[i], selector, action);  // Recursively call the function on each child node.
    }
}
```
This solution assumes you have an external library for random number generation and uses pthreads to manage concurrency. It also provides a basic structure for a DOM tree element and a recursive traversal function that takes in a selector function, performs an action if the selector returns true for any given node, and then recursively calls itself on each child of the current node.
"]

