["Here is a simple implementation of a function that creates and populates an array of structures. The use of dynamic memory allocation allows the list to be easily resized to handle varying values of N. A mutex lock is used to ensure thread safety when generating random numbers for MAC Data Block sizes in a multi-threaded scenario.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <pthread.h>

typedef struct mac_header {
    int header_type;
} MacHeader;

typedef struct lte_mac_data_block {
    int data_size;
} LTEMacDataBlock;

typedef struct lcg {
    int value;
} LCG;

typedef struct lte_mac_pdu {
    MacHeader header;
    LCG lcg;
    LTEMacDataBlock data_block;
} LTEMacPDU;

pthread_mutex_t mutex = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;

LTEMacPDU* create_mac_pdus(int N, int *error) {
    // Input validation
    if (N < 1 || N > 1000) {
        *error = 1;  // out of range error code
        return NULL;
    }

    LTEMacPDU* list = malloc(sizeof(LTEMacPDU) * N);
    if (list == NULL) {
        *error = 2;  // memory allocation failure error code
        return NULL;
    }

    for (int i = 0; i < N; ++i) {
        list[i].header.header_type = i % 3;  // Example data for MAC Header type
        list[i].lcg.value = i + 1;            // Example data for LCG value

        pthread_mutex_lock(&mutex);
        list[i].data_block.data_size = rand() % 1024;  // Random MAC Data Block size
        pthread_mutex_unlock(&mutex);
    }

    *error = 0;  // No error code
    return list;
}

void free_mac_pdus(LTEMacPDU* list) {
    free(list);
}
```
This implementation assumes a single-threaded environment for simplicity, but it's easy to adapt to a multi-threaded scenario with minor modifications. 

Note: This code does not handle error conditions in detail (like out of memory), this is just a simple example. In real-world use, you might want to add checks and return values indicating whether or not the operation was successful. Also, the rand() function is used here which isn't thread safe by itself, using a mutex ensures that it is safe in multi-threaded scenarios.
